course: dictionary
lesson: 7994
title: Recycling: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Recycling is a noun, and it can also show an action. To find its meaning, read the words around it. «Rubbish goes in the right bin: recycling, compost or general waste.» Here recycling names a bin, so it means a thing you put rubbish in.
explain: «Recycling works best for some materials.» Here recycling means the process of collecting used things and making them into new things. Check by swapping in "the process of" and reading the sentence again. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Greasy or dirty items can spoil a load of recycling.» The clue is spoil: a load is a batch, so recycling here means the used things that have been collected to be recycled. Words can have more than one meaning, so always read the clues before you decide.
explain: «Most of these minibeasts eat dead leaves and rotting wood, so they are the garden's recycling team, turning old plants back into soil.» Here recycling is like a job, and turning old plants into soil shows that it means making old things useful again.
fact: Recycling means collecting used things like paper, glass, metal and plastic and making them into new things.
fact: Recycling saves raw materials and energy, cuts pollution and means less rubbish in landfill.
fact: Bins are often colour-coded, but the rules differ by town, so check your local rules.
fact: Some things cannot go in recycling, like dirty food packaging, nappies and batteries. They need special collection.
fact: Recycling comes after «reduce» and «reuse» in the waste hierarchy.
exercise: «Greasy or dirty items can spoil a load of recycling.» In this sentence, a load of recycling means | A kind of rubbish lorry | *A batch of used things collected to be recycled | A pile of new paper | Dirty food packaging that goes in the bin
exercise: Which thing should NOT go in the recycling bin? | Glass jars | *Batteries, which need special collection | Clean paper | Plastic bottles
exercise: Which sentence uses recycling as an action? | The recycling bin is full. | The recycling symbol is on the lid. | The recycling centre is near the shops. | *We are recycling our old cans today.
test: «The recycling centre is near the shops.» What is a recycling centre? | A kind of waste truck | A shop that sells bins | A type of garden plant | *A place where used things are taken to be recycled
test: Which word means the process of making used things into new ones? | Landfill | Pollution | Compost | *Recycling
exam: Ella says recycling only means a bin. What is the best reply? | Yes, it means a shop | No, it only means rubbish | Yes, it only means a bin | *No, it can mean the process, the used things collected, or the action of recycling
